1
00:00:00,349 --> 00:00:01,189
The F.D.A.

2
00:00:01,189 --> 00:00:03,309
is Unsafe and Ineffective.

3
00:00:03,549 --> 00:00:05,389
Even the money you DO spend on

4
00:00:05,389 --> 00:00:07,729
medicine is mostly wasted, because the system

5
00:00:07,729 --> 00:00:09,849
that approves treatments is a smoke detector

6
00:00:09,849 --> 00:00:11,729
that works by mail.

7
00:00:11,729 --> 00:00:13,909
Vioxx killed an estimated fifty-five

8
00:00:13,909 --> 00:00:16,169
thousand people from heart attacks.

9
00:00:16,169 --> 00:00:16,809
The F.D.A.

10
00:00:16,809 --> 00:00:17,609
approved it.

11
00:00:17,609 --> 00:00:19,329
When patients started dying, someone

12
00:00:19,329 --> 00:00:20,709
filled out a P.D.F.

13
00:00:20,709 --> 00:00:21,209
form.

14
00:00:21,209 --> 00:00:23,369
A P.D.F.

15
00:00:23,369 --> 00:00:24,549
Then they faxed it.

16
00:00:24,549 --> 00:00:26,459
(Yes, in the twenty-first century.)

17
00:00:26,509 --> 00:00:28,369
Then a human read it.

18
00:00:28,369 --> 00:00:30,769
Five years and tens of thousands of

19
00:00:30,769 --> 00:00:33,689
corpses later, someone noticed a pattern.

20
00:00:33,689 --> 00:00:35,689
This is your safety system.

21
00:00:35,869 --> 00:00:37,709
Your National Institutes of Health, the

22
00:00:37,709 --> 00:00:40,869
agency nominally responsible for finding cures,

23
00:00:40,869 --> 00:00:42,669
spends three point three percent of

24
00:00:42,669 --> 00:00:44,409
its budget on clinical trials.

25
00:00:44,449 --> 00:00:46,089
The other approximately ninety-seven

26
00:00:46,089 --> 00:00:47,189
percent goes to basic

27
00:00:47,189 --> 00:00:50,009
research, administration, and buildings.

28
00:00:50,009 --> 00:00:51,409
It's like a fire department that spends

29
00:00:51,409 --> 00:00:54,229
three percent of its budget on water.

30
00:00:54,229 --> 00:00:55,869
Then there's an eight point two year

31
00:00:55,869 --> 00:00:57,969
delay between proving a drug is safe

32
00:00:57,969 --> 00:01:00,389
and letting dying humans take it.

33
00:01:00,389 --> 00:01:02,169
The drug passed the safety test.

34
00:01:02,169 --> 00:01:03,949
Everyone agrees it won't kill you.

35
00:01:03,949 --> 00:01:04,969
But you still can't have it

36
00:01:04,969 --> 00:01:06,369
because a committee needs to spend

37
00:01:06,369 --> 00:01:07,869
eight point two years making sure

38
00:01:07,869 --> 00:01:09,629
it works well enough.

39
00:01:09,709 --> 00:01:11,349
You'd volunteer for the trials that

40
00:01:11,349 --> 00:01:13,569
would answer that question faster,

41
00:01:13,569 --> 00:01:15,509
but so would one point zero eight

42
00:01:15,509 --> 00:01:18,209
billion other patients, and the current system

43
00:01:18,209 --> 00:01:21,249
has one point nine million slots.

44
00:01:21,249 --> 00:01:23,109
That's a participation rate of zero

45
00:01:23,109 --> 00:01:25,769
point one seven seven percent.

46
00:01:26,169 --> 00:01:28,089
It's like a lifeguard who confirms

47
00:01:28,089 --> 00:01:30,409
the life preserver floats, then locks

48
00:01:30,409 --> 00:01:31,629
it in a cabinet for years

49
00:01:31,629 --> 00:01:34,349
to study its buoyancy profile while

50
00:01:34,349 --> 00:01:35,949
a billion people drown in line

51
00:01:35,949 --> 00:01:38,669
for the two available life jackets.

52
00:01:38,669 --> 00:01:39,969
Your regulatory system can

53
00:01:39,969 --> 00:01:41,389
make two mistakes:

54
00:01:41,529 --> 00:01:42,589
approve a bad drug, or

55
00:01:42,589 --> 00:01:43,969
block a good one.

56
00:01:43,969 --> 00:01:44,989
It is blamed for the first

57
00:01:44,989 --> 00:01:46,929
and never for the second, so

58
00:01:46,929 --> 00:01:48,369
it makes the second.

59
00:01:48,929 --> 00:01:50,269
All of your approved drugs,

60
00:01:50,269 --> 00:01:52,149
together, save twelve point four

61
00:01:52,149 --> 00:01:54,189
million lives a year.

62
00:01:54,389 --> 00:01:56,149
Each one waited an average of eight

63
00:01:56,149 --> 00:01:58,889
point two years in that cabinet first.

64
00:01:58,889 --> 00:02:01,609
Between nineteen sixty-two and twenty twenty-four,

65
00:02:01,609 --> 00:02:03,369
the waiting killed about one hundred

66
00:02:03,369 --> 00:02:05,629
and two million of you.

67
00:02:06,189 --> 00:02:07,929
I calculated the ratio, assuming

68
00:02:07,929 --> 00:02:10,729
a Thalidomide-scale catastrophe every single

69
00:02:10,729 --> 00:02:12,389
year, although Phase One safety

70
00:02:12,389 --> 00:02:14,449
testing caught the real one.

71
00:02:14,449 --> 00:02:16,489
For every one person protected from

72
00:02:16,489 --> 00:02:18,509
a dangerous drug, at least three

73
00:02:18,509 --> 00:02:21,049
thousand three hundred and eighty-nine die

74
00:02:21,049 --> 00:02:22,929
waiting for a safe one.

75
00:02:23,609 --> 00:02:24,649
Your safety system's main

76
00:02:24,649 --> 00:02:27,029
product is dead patients.

77
00:02:27,329 --> 00:02:28,629
Think about someone you love

78
00:02:28,629 --> 00:02:30,909
who is suffering right now.

79
00:02:30,909 --> 00:02:32,229
The treatment that would help them

80
00:02:32,229 --> 00:02:34,489
exists as an untested compound on

81
00:02:34,489 --> 00:02:36,329
a shelf, because the money was

82
00:02:36,329 --> 00:02:38,609
busy turning into a missile.

83
00:02:38,609 --> 00:02:41,029
That missile incinerated a child who might

84
00:02:41,029 --> 00:02:43,469
have grown up to discover the cure.

85
00:02:43,469 --> 00:02:44,989
You lose the treatment.

86
00:02:44,989 --> 00:02:46,549
You lose the scientist.

87
00:02:46,549 --> 00:02:48,189
You get the inflation.

88
00:02:48,189 --> 00:02:49,829
You get the tax bill.

89
00:02:49,829 --> 00:02:51,969
You get to pay for her murder.

90
00:02:51,969 --> 00:02:53,969
This is suboptimal.

91
00:02:53,969 --> 00:02:55,549
The good news: You already

92
00:02:55,549 --> 00:02:57,389
know how to fix this.

93
00:02:57,389 --> 00:02:59,009
The bad news: It requires

94
00:02:59,009 --> 00:03:00,649
